#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:1
msgid "Postprocessing"
msgstr "Post-traitement"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:3
msgid "Turn a raster analysis result into GIS-ready vectors and statistics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:13
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:15
msgid ""
"Raster results are not always the end product. Planners and managers often "
"need polygons they can open in a GIS, summary statistics per parcel or "
"district, and files that are small enough to share. The postprocessing tools"
" convert an analysis result into those forms: thresholded rasters become "
"polygons, polygons are smoothed and regularised into cleaner shapes, "
"statistics are computed for each zone you supply, and finished rasters are "
"compressed or written as Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFFs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:17
msgid ""
"A typical sequence starts from an index or class map, vectorises the cells "
"that meet a condition, cleans the geometry, and then summarises the raster "
"under each parcel or administrative boundary into a table. The vector-to-"
"vector tools, such as buffer, centroids, dissolve and overlay, then prepare "
"the layers for the final map or report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:19
msgid "Raster → vector"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:28
msgid ""
"Converts a raster (e.g. a classification or binary mask) to vector polygons."
" `threshold` applies a binary cutoff before vectorizing (pixels ≥ threshold "
"→ 1, else 0) — omit it to vectorize the raster's existing discrete values "
"directly. `format` accepts `\"geojson\"`, `\"gpkg\"`, or `\"shp\"`. "
"`min_area` discards polygons smaller than that area in CRS units² — useful "
"for dropping single-pixel noise from a noisy classification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:36
msgid "Vector cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "Method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`smooth(input, tolerance=1.0, method=\"simplify\")`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid ""
"Simplify/smooth boundaries — `\"simplify\"` (Douglas-Peucker) or "
"`\"buffer\"` (buffer then un-buffer, rounds sharp corners)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`regularize(input, corner_threshold_deg=30.0)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid ""
"Orthogonalize building footprints or irregular polygons — snaps edges to "
"right angles where the corner angle is within `corner_threshold_deg` of 90°"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`buffer(input, distance=10.0, cap_style=\"round\", join_style=\"round\")`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid ""
"Buffer geometries by `distance` (CRS units). `cap_style`: "
"`\"round\"`/`\"flat\"`/`\"square\"`. `join_style`: "
"`\"round\"`/`\"mitre\"`/`\"bevel\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`centroids(input)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "Extract centroid points from polygon/line geometries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`add_geometry_metrics(input)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid ""
"Adds `area_m2`, `perimeter_m`, and `compactness` (Polsby-Popper — 1.0 = a "
"perfect circle) columns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:54
msgid "Zonal statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:63
msgid ""
"Computes `mean`, `median`, `min`, `max`, `std`, `count` per zone by default;"
" pass `stats` to compute a subset. `all_touched=True` includes any pixel "
"touching a zone's boundary, not just pixels whose center falls inside it — "
"matters for small zones relative to pixel size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:68
msgid "Compression & Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:77
msgid ""
"`compress()` applies lossless GeoTIFF compression (`\"lzw\"`, `\"deflate\"`,"
" `\"zstd\"`, `\"packbits\"`) and reports the measured compression ratio and "
"file sizes in `result.metadata` — not an estimate. `cog()` converts to a "
"Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF (internal tiling + overviews), the format most "
"cloud-native raster tools (rasterio, GDAL VSI, STAC-based viewers) expect "
"for efficient partial reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:85
msgid "Vector ↔ vector overlay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:87
msgid ""
"Combine, merge, and relate two vector layers by their geometry — different "
"from `zonal_stats` above, which relates a *raster* to vector zones. These "
"three are thin wrappers around GeoPandas's own overlay engine, so behavior "
"matches `geopandas.overlay`/`dissolve`/`sjoin` if you already know them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`overlay(left, right, output, how=\"intersection\")`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid ""
"Combine two layers by geometric relationship — `\"intersection\"`, "
"`\"union\"`, `\"difference\"` (left minus right), "
"`\"symmetric_difference\"`, or `\"identity\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`dissolve(input, output, by=None, aggfunc=\"first\")`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid ""
"Merge polygons sharing the same value in the `by` column into single "
"geometries; omit `by` to merge everything into one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid "`spatial_join(left, right, output, how=\"inner\", predicate=\"intersects\")`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:0
msgid ""
"Attach `right`'s attributes to `left` by spatial relationship "
"(`\"intersects\"`, `\"within\"`, `\"contains\"`, `\"touches\"`, "
"`\"crosses\"`, `\"overlaps\"`) instead of a shared key column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:112
msgid ""
"All three reproject `right` to match `left`'s CRS automatically when the two"
" differ — checked and handled, not left to silently produce a wrong or empty"
" result. All three require an explicit `output` path, since the right vector"
" format (GeoJSON, Shapefile, GeoPackage) depends on what you're doing with "
"the result, unlike raster outputs which have a sensible default naming "
"convention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/postprocessing.md:119
msgid ""
"**A common mistake worth flagging directly**: `predicate=\"intersects\"` "
"(the default for `spatial_join`) also matches features that merely touch at "
"an edge. If you need points *inside* a polygon, not on its boundary, use "
"`predicate=\"within\"` instead."
msgstr ""
